00:40:47.611 --> 00:40:53.551
Now, the thing about
these peaks is that these

00:40:53.551 --> 00:40:56.220
are called characteristic.

00:40:56.220 --> 00:41:00.257
And what's nice about them is,
in fact, that no matter what,

00:41:00.257 --> 00:41:01.892
they only depend--

00:41:01.892 --> 00:41:04.695
I don't care how much
energy I send in.

00:41:04.695 --> 00:41:08.799
These peaks only depend
on the metal atom.

00:41:08.799 --> 00:41:13.070
So Ronten put in a metal, and
he'd always get the same peaks

00:41:13.070 --> 00:41:15.573
if I give it enough energy.

00:41:15.573 --> 00:41:17.808
Maybe I don't have enough
energy to excite anything

00:41:17.808 --> 00:41:18.442
from down here.

00:41:18.442 --> 00:41:19.810
Then you don't get these peaks.

00:41:19.810 --> 00:41:21.579
You still get
Bremsstrahlung, but you don't

00:41:21.579 --> 00:41:23.547
get the characteristic peaks.

00:41:23.547 --> 00:41:25.449
They're called characteristic
because they're

00:41:25.449 --> 00:41:26.817
characteristic of the metal.

00:41:26.817 --> 00:41:28.752
Now they're dependent
on the chemistry.

00:41:28.752 --> 00:41:30.221
If I put in different
metal in, I'm

00:41:30.221 --> 00:41:32.490
going to get different Peaks

00:41:32.490 --> 00:41:34.992
And so with these
two types of X-rays,

00:41:34.992 --> 00:41:38.929
I've got a new kind of light
that I can shine on materials.

00:41:38.929 --> 00:41:41.065
I've got a new kind of
light that I can shine.

00:41:41.065 --> 00:41:43.501
And the light-- when I
plot it all together,

00:41:43.501 --> 00:41:53.410
it might look something like
this where maybe these are

00:41:53.410 --> 00:41:55.012
the peaks--

00:41:55.012 --> 00:41:55.779
uh oh.

00:41:55.779 --> 00:41:56.480
OK.

00:41:56.480 --> 00:41:59.483
Maybe these are the peaks
due to going down to K,

00:41:59.483 --> 00:42:02.486
and these are the ones
due to going down to L.

00:42:02.486 --> 00:42:08.425
So those are K, and these are
L. and the rest is continuous,

00:42:08.425 --> 00:42:09.793
and they're on
top of each other.

00:42:09.793 --> 00:42:11.061
And I get it all.

00:42:11.061 --> 00:42:13.797
But with that new kind of
light, I can do new things.

00:42:13.797 --> 00:42:14.865
And that's very important.

